/* tx-pathway: the treatment pathway after diagnosis, for young people (6 to 17) and adults.
   Collections: txSequence (NICE order), txPlanItems (support before and alongside medicine), txCardiac (NG87 1.7.5
   heart history and the 1.7.4 ECG item), txCautions (contraindication and caution screen; ids are used by
   txDrugs.ci / txDrugs.caution; each item has a `group` heading for the screen, listed in display order), txSideEffects (asked at each review), txCounsel (counselling checklist),
   txRxChecks (prescription checklist), txMonitor (schedules, action thresholds, annual review, hand-back,
   shared care and transition).
   Optional filters on items: ages ('young' | 'adult' | 'all'), ageMin, ageMax (years, inclusive), drugs ([drug ids]).
   `hist` lists workspace history item ids (js/data/history.js) that pre-fill a "yes" (shown as "From history").
   `risk` (txCautions) lists Safety and risk step item ids (history.js `risk.items`) that pre-fill a "yes" in the
   same way (shown as "From the safety step"). Only close matches are linked; every item must still be answered
   by the clinician.
   txPlanItems: `conditional: true` with `when` ('oddcd': oppositional or conduct symptoms recorded; 'medhelps':
   medicine started and helping while impairment remains; 'medication': medicine is planned, that is the plan
   decision is not non-drug support only or a referral) marks an item that counts only when it applies.
   tp_recheck is the gate before medicine (the view asks for confirmation when the findings disagree).
   txCautions: ci_hepatic 'yes' brings up the Child-Pugh question, stored as treatment.baseline.childPugh
   ('A' | 'B' | 'C'; the engine reduces atomoxetine doses for B and C). ci_cyp3a4 (inhibitor or inducer in
   one item) was replaced by ci_cyp3a4_inh and ci_cyp3a4_ind; the engine still reads ci_cyp3a4 in older
   records. A product may add its own contraindications (txProducts `ci`, for example ci_acidsuppress).
   txSideEffects: `urgent: true` means any report, even mild, needs same-day action (the review raises an
   urgent flag and the dose is not increased).
   txMonitor: `field` names where the last check is found: a review measure ('heightCm', 'weightKg', 'bp') or a
   date kept in treatment.monitor ('needReviewDate', 'annualDate'). `specialistOnly: true` items stay with the
   specialist team and are left out of the GP's shared care table (AA.treatment.sharedCarePlan).
   Ids are stored in assessment records: never rename or reuse an id; add new items at the end of a list.
   Sources: NICE NG87 (2018, updated 2019; clause numbers checked against the live text 25 Oct 2026);
   NICE NG136 (updated 26 Feb 2026); NICE NG43; NICE NG46; Misuse of Drugs Regulations 2001 regs 15–16;
   Human Medicines Regulations 2012; emc SmPCs (see tx-products.js); SPS (28 Aug 2025);
   NHS England national shared care protocol for atomoxetine in adults (v1, July 2022); GMC 0–18 years;
   main course Modules 3, 5, 6, 7 and 9. Lines marked "Clinical practice" are not from a named source. */

